// Title: Registry Entries For Azorult Malware
// Sigma ID: f7f9ab88-7557-4a69-b30e-0a8f91b3a0e7
// Status: test | Level: critical
// Author: Trent Liffick
// Date: 2020-05-08 | Modified: 2021-11-27
// ATT&CK: persistence, execution, defense-impairment, T1112
// Description: Detects the presence of a registry key created during Azorult execution
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.trendmicro.com/vinfo/us/threat-encyclopedia/malware/trojan.win32.azoruit.a
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/registry/registry_event/registry_event_mal_azorult.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 1 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)SYSTEM.*$" and RegistryKey endswith "\\services\\localNETService"
